pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The `+` sibling of `wcnf_literal_spelling_alias`, and the nastier case: the
% proof never names the ghost variable `x+1` at all, the solution-hint growing
% supplies it. The two hard clauses are x1 and ~x1 over one variable, so the
% instance is infeasible and no solution may be logged.
f 2;
sol ~x1;
output NONE;
conclusion BOUNDS 0 0;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
